    "answer": {
      "short": "Rises in temperature, from top to bottom: $15,\\ 20,\\ 22,\\ 5,\\ 2,\\ 13,\\ 18\\ ^\\circ\\mathrm{C}$.",
      "worked": "Rise in temperature = final temperature − initial temperature.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}5-(-10)&=5+10\\\\5-(-10)&=15\\,{}^\\circ\\mathrm{C}\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}5-(-15)&=5+15\\\\5-(-15)&=20\\,{}^\\circ\\mathrm{C}\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}-3-(-25)&=-3+25\\\\-3-(-25)&=22\\,{}^\\circ\\mathrm{C}\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}-15-(-20)&=-15+20\\\\-15-(-20)&=5\\,{}^\\circ\\mathrm{C}\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}-5-(-7)&=-5+7\\\\-5-(-7)&=2\\,{}^\\circ\\mathrm{C}\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}2-(-11)&=2+11\\\\2-(-11)&=13\\,{}^\\circ\\mathrm{C}\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}5-(-13)&=5+13\\\\5-(-13)&=18\\,{}^\\circ\\mathrm{C}\\end{align*}$$",
